WORK
  TYGARIA, comprising: the MULTIVERSE of that name -- the connected set of
  worlds, realms and planes described across the three volumes, together with
  their lore, cosmology, place names, histories and characters; its realisation
  as a PERSISTENT VIRTUAL WORLD in which members are present as their own
  characters; the three-volume work of fiction that establishes it; and a
  computer game set within it -- together with all of their source code,
  compiled builds, artwork, cover art, character designs and names, logos,
  music, sound effects, level, world and environment designs, user-interface
  designs, and the complete text of all three volumes (together, "the Work").

  The multiverse is named first deliberately, and named as a multiverse rather
  than a world. What the volumes establish is not one setting but a connected
  set of them, so the Work is not limited to any single world within it, to the
  worlds realised in software to date, or to those the volumes describe in the
  greatest detail. The game and the volumes are each expressions of it; the
  virtual world is where it is inhabited rather than only read or played; and
  further expressions, in any medium and in any world of the multiverse, are
  equally part of the Work.

